<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Remarks">Remarks</span></h2>
<p>To tell the game to use the values in this table, set the area's <b>AREA_ID</b> variable to the appropriate <b>ID</b> from this table.
</p><p>One of the uses for the areadata 2da is creature scaling. When the player enters an area, the creatures in the area are scaled to Player's level provided it is within the <b>MinLevel</b> and <b>MaxLevel </b>values specified for the area. For example if <b>MaxLevel </b>is set to 5 and a level 8 Player enters, the game engine will scale the creatures to level 5. The creature's rank is a secondary scale applied after the level scaling.
</p>
